cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenFocus in your work, please cite it as below. See also the repository README for algorithm-specific references."
title: OpenFocus
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xinzhe
    family-names: Xie
    email: xiexinzheyyy@163.com
    affiliation: Zhejiang University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xinzhe99/OpenFocus"
url: "https://github.com/Xinzhe99/OpenFocus"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23050823
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI — always resolves to the latest versioned release"
abstract: >-
  OpenFocus is an open-source multi-focus image fusion workstation for
  PyQt6-based desktop use and headless command-line pipelines. It combines
  fast similarity, homography and ECC image registration with ten fusion
  algorithms (guided filter, DCT, dual-tree complex wavelet transform,
  GFG-FGF, StackMFF V1/V2/V3 and OpenFocus A/B/C), supports 8- and
  16-bit stacks, HEIC input, source-locked retouching, batch processing and
  project files, and ships for Windows and macOS (Apple Silicon) as well as
  through PyPI (`pip install openfocus`).
keywords:
  - image fusion
  - focus stacking
  - multifocus
  - microscopy
  - macro photography
  - image registration
  - ECC
  - PyQt6
